course: dictionary
lesson: 562
title: Audition
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An audition is a short performance that shows whether you are good enough for a part in a play, a band, a choir or a show. «In an audition people try out, and the director chooses who fits each part.» So an audition is a try-out, and the director is the person who makes the choice.
explain: Audition can also be a verb, meaning to do that try-out, or to watch and judge people doing it. «A school play starts with auditions, where everyone tries out.» Look for the clue words: try out, choose, part. They tell you the meaning.
explain: Small parts matter too. «Every part, even "Tree Number 3", is needed to tell the story.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An audition is a short performance that shows whether you are good enough for a part.
fact: As a noun it is «an audition» and as a verb it is «to audition» or «auditioning».
fact: You can «go to an audition», «audition for a part» or «pass the audition».
fact: In a formal, science sense, «audition» means the sense of hearing.
fact: Many famous actors started with tiny roles, so a small part can be a great start.
exercise: «In an audition people try out, and the director chooses who fits each part.» What is an audition? | A kind of costume for the stage | *A short performance to show if you are good enough for a part | A long holiday by the sea | A school lunch menu
exercise: Ruby says, «I will audition for the school play.» What does audition mean here? | To fall asleep on stage | To eat a snack before lunch | To paint the scenery | *To do a try-out performance to show you are good enough
exercise: Which phrase means you did well enough at your try-out? | Skipped the audition | Forgot the audition | *Passed the audition
test: Copy the word from «A school play starts with auditions, where everyone tries out» that is the plural of audition. | everyone | starts | school | *auditions
test: Tom asks what «audition» means in a science lesson about the body. What is the answer? | A small role in a film | *The sense of hearing | A type of music for a choir | A kind of stage light
exam: Ana says, «Every part, even "Tree Number 3", is needed to tell the story.» What does this suggest about auditions? | Parts are chosen by the audience, not the director | Only the lead actor matters | Tree Number 3 is the star of every play | *Even small parts matter to the story
